# The interdental, which Catalan has not got, is an alveolar nasal now.
#
# Castilian velarises an n at the end of a word and Catalan does not: gran is
# [g r a n], not [g r a ng]. The change is made in span_phrase_level_rules,
# 588 lines that do a great deal else besides, and it is made on the phone's
# code -- so a word-final n that is some other code goes through untouched.
#
# T is that other code. Castilian spells it with c before e and i and with z,
# and Catalan says a plain s for both, so nothing here can reach it: it is a
# code the language cannot say, with an arm already in every chain that asks
# about a phoneme, which the docs' own advice prefers to a code that has never
# existed. Its record now says what n's says -- voiced, nasal, alveolar -- so
# every rule that reads the record rather than the code treats it as one.
#
# What it sounds like is what n sounds like, so this forwards. Bare, because
# it stands where a rule the value chain calls stands and the choice points
# around the call are the chain's.
rule span_ph_T takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  bare
  call span_ph_n
end

# And the velar fricative all but says nothing, because it is not a sound of
# Catalan's any more: st_phone.up turns a word-final r into it and this is where that r
# stops being heard. Castilian reaches this phone from j and from g before e
# and i, and Catalan says the voiced postalveolar for both, so nothing else in
# the module can arrive here.
#
# Laying nothing down was not the same as leaving a gap, and that turned out
# to be exactly what it was. The formant targets are whatever the segment
# before set, so the vowel does carry through -- but the amplitude is not a
# formant, and with nothing setting it the segment came out silent. Twenty
# milliseconds of silence between two words is a stop closure: carrer venir
# had one in the middle of it where casa venir has none, and a listener heard
# the b of amb in the same place before that rule stopped using this phone.
#
# So it sets an amplitude of its own, low enough to be the tail of the vowel
# rather than a sound. 30 at thirty milliseconds is what the ear and the
# measurement agreed on over four settings: below it the silence comes back --
# at 20 the gap in carrer venir returns -- and above it the vowel stops
# fading and holds, 45 sitting at a fifth of full amplitude for the whole
# segment. What that buys at the end of an utterance is the fall a word-final
# vowel gets and a word ending in this phone did not: venir stopped dead where
# veni fades over sixty milliseconds, and now it fades too.
#
# The frame and the fence are the rule's own, as syneresis's are.
rule span_ph_j takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2754 to 30
  match
end
